SUMMARY:Vice City - Fortitude Valley True Crime Tour
DESCRIPTION:Tickets for Vice City - Fortitude Valley True Crime Tour in Bri
 sbane 🎫 Walking Tour Ticket for 1 Adult (18+) 🎫 Walking Tour Ticket 
 for 1 Child (0–17) Highlights 🚶 A true crime guided walking tour of B
 risbane’s Fortitude Valley and its infamous past 🤫 Revisit locations 
 for underworld activity from the 70s and 80s red light district 🔎 Uncov
 er the tales of corruption\, glitz and glamour General Info 📅 Date: var
 ious Saturdays (select during purchase) 🕒 Time: 4.30 pm ⏳ Duration: 9
 0–100 minutes 📍 Meeting point: Meet at the corner of Church St & Wick
 ham St\, next to the Holy Trinity Church. 👤 Age requirement: all ages w
 elcome ♿ Accessibility: this event is wheelchair accessible. Although th
 e regular route could be slightly altered in order to accommodate (it may 
 take an extra 5-10 minutes to complete). 📱 Please see your Fever ticket
  & confirmation email for all essential post-purchase information Descript
 ion Travel to the Fortitude Valley\, a rough and tumble place where the li
 ghts of Fortitude Valley shone the brightest during its most corrupt era. 
 Forget the fake news stories\, and join your tour guide for a memorable tr
 ip down the glamourous\, glitzy and corruption-laden past. Visit the headq
 uarters of the Underworld Kingpins of the 1980s and experience a taste of 
 the findings from the infamous Fitzgerald Inquiry. Get your tickets now fo
 r Vice City - Fortitude Valley True Crime Tour in Brisbane!
LOCATION:Church St and Wickham St\, Fortitude Valley
URL:https://feverup.com/m/631444
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:brisbane-pf87s5@dothings
DTSTART;TZID=Australia/Brisbane:20260912T170000
DTEND;TZID=Australia/Brisbane:20260912T180000
SUMMARY:Diagnonsense (improv comedy)
DESCRIPTION:Brisbane's best improv comedy! Come see Brisbane's funniest and
  most endearing disabled and chronically ill improvisers do funny make-em-
 ups on stage for your entertainment. We know better than most that laughte
 r isn't actually the best medicine\, but it sure can ease the load of movi
 ng through a world that wasn't built for you. Diagnonsense is scheduled at
  an early evening showtime to help you manage your spoons. Head home early
  if you're spent or hang around for more hilarious comedy with Big Fork Th
 eatre's regular Saturday Night Comedy programming. Big Fork Theatre is a f
 ully accessible venue. The corner entrance to the building is stair-free\,
  there's an elevator that will bring you up to the second floor and the fl
 exible seating in our theatre can be adapted to accommodate any needs. Str
 obe lighting will never be used in a Diagnonsense show. Personal accommoda
 tions (headphones\, stimming\, etc) are welcome\, we just ask that you res
 pect the performers' needs and limit talking/vocal expression while the ca
 st is performing. Laughing is encouraged of course! Please reach out of yo
 u have any particular accessibility needs you'd like accommodated. We can'
 t promise everything will be possible but we'll always try. Diagnonsense i
 s brought to you by a Little Spoons\, a group of Big Fork Theatre communit
 y members living with disability and chronic illness. Through these shows\
 , we hope to grow the visible representation of disability and chronic ill
 ness on Brisbane performing arts and comedy stages. In the process we migh
 t just happen to break down some stigmas\, challenge some internalised abl
 eism and encourage more inclusive practices across the arts. But no pressu
 re! TICKETS ARE ONLY $10 ONLINE | $15 ON THE DOOR
LOCATION:Big Fork Theatre\, 252 Saint Pauls Terrace
URL:https://www.bigforktheatre.com/shows-events/zlc325x7ttpk7rz-9wrxf-r76dd
END:VEVENT
