BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:brisbane-13flg1@dothings
DTSTART;TZID=Australia/Brisbane:20250621T100000
DTEND;TZID=Australia/Brisbane:20250621T120000
SUMMARY:Great and Small
DESCRIPTION:Animals have played a central part in Aboriginal and Torres Str
 ait Islander culture and spiritual beliefs for over 60\,000 years. Native 
 fauna form an integral part of relationships with Country\, in community a
 nd are a foundation of economies\, identity and sustainability. Over many 
 millennia of co-existence animals have been central to survival as a food 
 source\, for First Nations people they are also absorbed into lore and cul
 ture as images of totemic power\; and into the ancestral creation stories 
 that link people\, land and animals. ‘Great and small’ is a celebratio
 n of these connections.
LOCATION:QAG\, Stanley Place\, South Bank
URL:https://www.qagoma.qld.gov.au/exhibition/great-and-small
END:VEVENT
